should i go green  should you spend the time effort money  to make your company a green company i  got a great question from one of my  youtube viewers love you guys corona  wrote in to say would you purchase  clothes clothes made from recycled  plastic bottles  or do you think customers would care  about these positive impact it has on  the world  so first of all that's cool i've never  heard of a of a clothing that's made out  of recycled plastic bottles that's  pretty funky  but here's my answer for you and for  anybody who's thinking about should i  introduce a new green initiative or a  new social initiative  when it comes to those kind of important  decisions for your business i always  approach it from a position of  doing it to do it instead of doing it  for marketing reasons  typically if you just look at the stats  you can charge 20 to 30 percent more if  it's green or if it has a social angle  there is a little bit of a premium that  people will pay if they know that there  is a social component to it  but i would never say do it because of  that because it's not going to be  genuine people will see through it if  you're doing something  only to try to make more money  people have a pretty high bs meter and  they're gonna see right through it so  what i say to you  is do it to do it do it because it's the  right thing to do if this is what you  believe in if you believe in in green  business and entrepreneurs have a  responsibility to make our world a  better place and this is how you're  going to do it if that's your belief  then you do it  regardless of the impact it's going to  have with your customers you do it  because it's the right thing to do  and if that's why you're doing it  customers will come on board and they'll  believe it and they'll want to be part  of the movement that you're helping  create  does that make sense  when you are  only marketing something because you're  trying to make money  customers won't buy from you i had a  great ques